  "scope": "Consent/account boundaries and truthful outcomes for existing Input learning; not calibration or whole-system acceptance.",
  "behavior": [
    "Local authorization sidecars bind each optional outcome to one account session and exact consent grant. Wire carries only the grant timestamp as admission metadata; actor is authenticated server-side and absent from stored task aggregates.",
    "Withdrawal invalidates queued and pending requests before token lookup; token identity must match the action-time owner. Account A to B to A never restores old queued authorization.",
    "Account-local failed-withdrawal hold survives restart when storage succeeds. Per-account intent revisions, ordered storage writes and a compensating hold prevent a late grant response/native storage removal from erasing a newer withdrawal. Network writes start in intent order; no new retry timer or app polling.",
    "Settings distinguish local pause, acknowledged account withdrawal, verified erasure and unknown erasure. Only literal countersErased=true claims deletion. Enabled or unstamped opposite-state responses remain pending with explicit retry.",
    "4029 serializes consent/flag admission and counter/aggregate writes using SHARE row locks, and rejects missing/stale grant provenance. Legacy overloads fail closed; core assistance is independent.",
    "4032 prevents retained learning under old disclosures from influencing ranking. Sole production personal-counter reader is gateway to attachOutcomeMemory to input_outcome_memory; erasure/expiry writers and service-only aggregated metrics remain separate.",
    "Aggregate RPC failures/unknown receipts are failed operations, not policy refusals. Ingest returns503 with actual committed/failed/refused counts. Client does not start a telemetry retry loop."
  ],
